/* ---------- Settings ---------- */
const APP_VER=210;
const WHATS_NEW=['Polish: dark mode fixes across Studio, Calendar and Tasks, a cleaner Working hours sheet, overnight shifts that carry into the next morning, imported calendars that handle moved events and repeats like the 2nd Tuesday, and tapping anywhere on a setting row flips its switch.','Make it yours: light or dark mode, five palettes plus your own color, title font, background, density, date format and bottom bar labels. Working hours now handle several jobs, shifts and flexible schedules with a reminder to add hours. Bring in Google, iCloud or Outlook calendars in Settings › Connections, and every reminder lives on one Notifications page.','Catch-up reviews you can do or skip, a weekly review switch, weeks that start on any day, Turn all on or off for an area’s modules, area icons in more places, a Tasks line under your priorities, and a simpler Data & help.','Sorting has its own icon, sheets put Why it matters right under the title, repeat and day pickers use the full width with Every day, Weekdays and Weekends shortcuts, Estimate, Energy and Where are gone, durations use a stopwatch, and folds open smoothly.','Modules are even quieter: an empty section is one Add row instead of a big card, one-time hints and footnotes are gone, and area pages only show tiles that have data.','Life areas and modules are quieter: area pages lead with one headline, show at most two previews and one suggestion, and numbers only speak up when something moved. Module pages drop taglines, repeated counts and all-is-well labels.','A quieter app: rows show only what you act on, long lists fold after the first rows, page titles size to fit, and Details show only what you filled in. Today and Calendar say repeated things once.','Project, goal, routine and list pages are calmer: one card with progress and rows, done items folded away, and details as simple rows. Inbox ideas sit on one line with a suggested type, Tidy up leads with its best guess, and the add sheets show details up front.','Organize pages match Tasks and Habits: no counts next to titles, the same slim Add bar, sticky view and area chips (tap to add or remove), and Projects and Goals grouped by life area in cards you can fold, each project as one compact row with its next task to tick. Inbox folds old-idea review into Tidy up, Lists lose the ⋯ on every row, and Routines lose an extra label.','Trips on the calendar: trip days get a blue outline with a plane on the first day, the name sits once under the week, a countdown card shows the next trip (or “Day 2 of 3” while you’re away), and Week view marks each trip day with a band.','Calendar is easier to read: habits no longer make every day look full on the heat map, all-day dots sit under the date instead of over it, each month in Quarter has its own weekday row, the day panel counts plans and habits separately, and an unset focus is a small “Set a focus” link.','Quick capture › More shows a card for each life area, and every choice has its module’s icon. Vague names like Entry and Item now say which module they belong to.','Ticking is quicker: a to-do fills and folds away in about half a second, and a habit ring fills in place without the page jumping. Habits get their own icons and colors (water drop, moon for no phone at night, and so on), and Water and Night join the icon picker.','Today is back to separate cards (to-dos, habits, schedule, tomorrow) with the slim rows. Ticked to-dos fold away smoothly. Items you open rather than tick, like reviewing cards or replacing a product, show their area icon and a › instead of a circle, so it’s clear what you’re checking off. Habit rings stay put while you tap. On a phone, stretching an event now needs a short hold, so scrolling can’t resize it. Product and other forms are tidier.','Habit icons only come from the set you can pick in New habit. The Workout done sheet and the New habit color and icon panel are better spaced.','Today is one quiet card: priorities, Also today, habits, schedule and tomorrow under thin labels. To-dos are one line: an ! in the circle for important, a time on the right if it has one, and a ⌄ to open steps. Hold a to-do and drag it onto a ring to make it a priority. Habits are a row of rings you tap to log.','Habits top is tighter: a slimmer Add a habit, less space between rows, and Collapse all / Expand all sits at the end of the All / Today chips.','Habit areas look cleaner: the area icon sits inside its progress ring with “1 of 3 done today” under the name, and Expand all / Collapse all opens or folds every area at once.','All habits are grouped by life area: each area is a card with a ring for how much of it you’ve done today, and tapping its name folds it away.','All habits is tighter: two lines per habit (name and 30-day percent, then the week’s dots, how often and the streak), and the legend and footnote are gone.','All habits: tick a habit done right from the list, and the percent and streak line up in one column on the right. “1 times a week” now reads “Once a week”.','Habits opens on All. Tap Today or Paused to add it to the filter and tap again to remove it, like Tasks; area chips work the same way.','Habits polish: count habits at their goal show a check and “8/8”, every-day habits show their day streak, habits group by time of day when you set one, a habit’s page shows This week first and Plan a session sits under the title, moving a planned session happens in the same sheet, and chip rows fade at the edge so you can tell they scroll.','Habits is calmer: one line per habit with “2 of 5 this week” and its streak, finished habits fold into Done, the header matches Tasks (view and area chips), every-day habits don’t ask to be planned, Workouts linking only shows on exercise habits, and Done today becomes “✓ Done today · Undo”.','Tasks: swipe chores and bills right to finish or left to open, sort by due date, priority or newest from the ··· menu, Done respects your area filter, and Add a task shows its shortcuts (! #home fri 9am) while you type.','Tasks has an On hold filter for to-dos in paused projects, grouped by project with a Resume button. The note at the bottom is gone.','Overdue sheet: choose Replan or Mark complete at the top. Replan only selects to-dos that can move (chores, repeats and deadlines are grayed); Mark complete can select anything.','In Replan, items that can only be marked done (chores, repeats, deadlines) are grayed, with a short note above the buttons.','Replan is a pick list now: everything overdue is selected (or just the one you tapped), tap to add or remove, then Mark done or Move to Today, Tomorrow, the weekend, next week, a date or Someday. Chores, missed repeats and past deadlines can be marked done there too.','The full demo is rebuilt without repeats: each example (like CRA or Workday Pro) appears once, and demo to-dos don’t repeat titles. Your own data was never affected.','Tasks: Overdue is sorted by due date, oldest first, with chores and bills mixed in by their date. The Add a task row is slimmer; tap its + for the full form.','Tasks is cleaner: area filters are just your life areas (Career, Home, Health…), Overdue only holds things whose date has passed (not ones due in a few days), life-area items take one line (“29 days overdue · Home · Chore”), and the title shows “21 today · 24 overdue” to match the filters.','Ticking the last step inside a to-do’s edit sheet now finishes the to-do, like it does on Today. Habit cards are snug, with no empty gap above Log today.','Small polish: all-day items and the + sit on one swipeable line, and very long to-do titles stop at three lines on Today (open it to see the rest).','Missed repeats (like rent from last week) and past-deadline to-dos now count in Overdue instead of Also today. Tap Overdue to mark a missed one done or skip it. The step ring around multi-step to-dos is no longer cut off.','Focus is calmer: a short white sheet with your priority on top (tap it to switch), a small timer you set with − and +, one Start button and Mark done underneath.','Focus lets you pick any open priority (switching saves the time you spent). Dragging onto a ring is smoother: the row fades, a pill lifts above your finger, the nearest ring pulls it in and says Make #2 or Replace #2, and it glides into place. Overdue now sits between + and More. Demo habits show proper icons.','A lighter Today card: Focus is a small play button by the count, overdue is a small red link beside Also today (tap to replan), and More and + are small buttons at the bottom. See full day now shows the whole day at full height, so the page scrolls straight through it, with no Now button popping up. Every habit shows an icon, and the first habit card keeps its margin.','One list on Today: chores, bills, meds and upkeep show as to-dos with their area icon and type. Overdue is one red row with Replan and See all, Also today shows three with “more today” to Tasks, and anything (done ones too) can be dragged onto a ring. Up next is replaced by a Focus button that opens a timer sheet you can edit, pause and finish from. Tasks has multi-select filters (Overdue, Today, Next 7 days, Anytime) and area chips under a header that stays put, with Replan on overdue.','Today is calmer at the bottom: the Inbox count stays on its badge, lessons live in Personal growth, and From your life areas matches the other cards.','A calmer Today: leftovers from earlier days are one row (Review or Move all), finished to-dos fold into Done and can still be dragged onto a ring, steps finish their task, overlapping events are tagged, and the Inbox nudge and lesson share one card.','The full demo is loaded: every day this month, every area and every module has data. Clear it any time from Data & help › Getting started.','Data & help › Getting started › Load the full demo fills every area and module with realistic data. Clear the full demo puts everything back.','The priorities card is titled “Today’s priorities”, with a little more room under the rings.','New Today card: your three priorities are rings. Tap one to mark it done, hold for options, or drag a to-do onto a ring. The next one shows as Up next with focus and done buttons, and other to-dos fold away.','Deleting a module you built suggests turning it off instead, like areas do.','Life areas and Modules are one place now: Settings › Life areas, then tap an area to turn it on or off, pick its modules, or build your own.','Deleting a custom area suggests turning it off instead, and Undo brings it back if you do delete.','Every day looks the same: Priorities, Other and Schedule on today, tomorrow and any future date.','Custom areas: tap one to rename it, pick its icon, or delete it. New areas get an icon too.','Custom areas have their own list in Settings › Life areas. Tap one to rename or delete it.','Life areas are listed A to Z.','What’s new moved off Today. It now waits in your Inbox, with a small dot on the Inbox button until you’ve seen it.','Section headers (like Health or Home on Modules) stay pinned at the top while you scroll through them.','Settings home is just names now.','Settings reorganized: Life areas sits with Modules, your plan is ordered by how often you use it, Week starts on moved to Planning, and Erase all data now lives at the very bottom.','Counters roll cleanly even when you tap quickly. Life areas show their icons in Settings. Quiet hours now sits with Notifications, and Check for updates moved to About.','Counters roll cleanly even when you tap quickly.','Fewer interruptions: Undo only appears after deleting, clearing, archiving or changing several things at once. Switches, checks, pins and priorities just change, with no message.','Modules is cleaner: just names and switches.','Smoother controls everywhere: switches glide without the page jumping, rows that depend on a switch fold in and out, segmented choices slide in sheets too, and every + / − counter rolls its number the same way.','Every module has its own icon. Fixed switches on Today & reviews that wouldn’t flip (and the page that wouldn’t open). Settings pages are tidier: one Working hours row, a single Help guide, and module rows only say what matters.','Reordering in sheets (Bottom bar, steps, pinned and more) now feels like Today: the row lifts, the others slide aside, and it settles into place.','Personalized foundation has a Finish setup button, so you can close the checklist without doing every step. Bring it back any time from Data & help.','Settings is reorganized into seven pages: Planning & availability; Tasks, habits & capture; Today & reviews; Calendar & sync; Life areas; Display & motion; Data & help. A search box at the top jumps straight to any setting.','Numbers that change when you tap, like a habit target or a count, now roll instead of snapping.','Data & help shows when you last backed up, with Export now. Help topics open one at a time. Example data hides once you have your own.','Modules has All, On and Off filters with one-line descriptions. Calendar link options are tucked into one row.','Every on/off switch now glides, everywhere: Settings, Modules, Life areas and every sheet. Before, switches on pages that redraw snapped instead of sliding.','Settings rows that appear when you switch something on, like Prompt from or Quiet hours times, now grow in smoothly. The bottom bar choices drop Insights and add Life Areas.','Habits shows each count once: the line by the title and the Done and Planned counts on each habit. Tasks’ add row has a Details button for the full form instead of a pencil.','Settings is shorter: just the names on its main page, full titles that fit, and the setup checklist disappears once you finish it.','Life Areas shows the areas you use. The rest wait behind a “more areas” link at the bottom.','Area pages are calmer: modules show just their name until they have something in them, empty Resources is a single line, and the extra buttons in the empty card are gone when Fill this in is showing.','The Learning Review module is now called Flashcards. Year in review lives only in Reviews, and Help is up to date.','Insights now lives inside Reviews, under the scorecard, once there’s a week of history. The scorecard waits for real numbers instead of showing zeros.','Pinned shortcuts on More no longer carry count badges. Long page titles like Recently deleted fit on one line, and a few descriptive subtitles are gone.','More is one page now: Organize, Reviews, Insights and Life Areas sit right on it. The Organize, Reflect and Discover pages and the Recent list are gone; area pages still suggest their own modules.','Empty pages show their message right away instead of a blank box first. An empty Archive skips its count and filters.','More is cleaner: Browse all, Kept, Organize, Reflect and Life Areas show just the names, without the line underneath.','Tools & Resources is gone. Each life area now has a Resources section for its links, notes and photos, with Open for links. Anything without an area waits at the bottom of Life Areas.','Templates live where you make things: New list, New routine and New project show your saved templates first. Press and hold one to delete it. Search finds them too.','Recently deleted: Empty all now sits at the top, and Select lets you pick several items to restore or delete for good at once.','Uncheck a priority after finishing all three and the Today card dissolves smoothly from green back to white.','Habit rings now fill slowly on iPhone too, gliding over about a second and a half when you check a habit off or undo it.','Finish all three priorities and the whole Today card turns green, fading in with a sheen.','Habit rings fill and empty slowly, like the progress bar does when you finish a task.','Checking off a habit card is smooth now: the ring fills, the card fades into its color with one soft glow, then glides to the end of the row without the page redrawing.','The “What should I do now?” card is gone from Today.','Dragging tasks on Today works like reordering your Top 3: the row lifts and the others slide out of the way as you move it, including across the Priorities line.','Moving or reordering something no longer pops up a message with Undo, anywhere in the app.','Checking off a habit card fills its ring, fades the card into its color with a soft glow, then slides it to the end of the row.','The Today card has two parts: Priorities and Other. Drag any task by its handle into Priorities to make it #1, #2 or #3; the old #3 drops back into Other. Drag a priority below the line to take it out.','Swipe right on any task to finish it, or left to edit it. Priorities work the same way.','Habits are now a row of cards you can swipe through. Log one and it slides to the end and turns solid in its own color.','Your Top 3 and to-dos now share one Today card: priorities sit at the top with their numbers, everything else follows, and nothing shows twice. One count and progress bar covers it all.','Habit rings take each habit’s own color, with its icon centred inside. Change both from the habit’s Appearance setting.','Coming up stays quiet when folded. The Now marker and line show when you open the full day.','A calmer Today that puts what matters first: your Top 3, a To-do card with its own progress bar, a Habits card with progress rings, and Coming up with your next few blocks. Tap See full day to open the time grid right there.','The date reads as one line now, all-day items sit as chips right under the week, and the add buttons are gone from the top. Add a to-do from its card, an all-day item from the + chip, or use the + button.','Workouts, Hevy-style: routines hold exercises with sets, reps, weight and a rest timer per exercise. Mark sets as warm-up, drop set or to failure, pair exercises into supersets, and tag each one with its main and supporting muscles.','Link a habit to your Workouts log: logging a workout or finishing a routine checks it off, checking it off logs a workout, and the log uses the habit’s target. Link Push, Pull and Legs and they take turns; Start always picks the one you’ve gone longest without.','Workouts shows your routine balance and which muscles you’ve trained over the last 30 days.','Weekly habit planning reads simply: Done and Planned counts above the day chips, and tapping a day no longer pops up a message.','Weekly habits now show a round chip for every day left this week. Tap one to plan it on that day, tap again to take it off.','Plan or move a habit session: tap Plan a session on any habit, or press and hold a habit under This week on Today to do it today, set a time, or pick another day.','Every sheet you type in now opens full height and stays still while the keyboard comes up, across the whole app.','Every add or save message across the app now has a › to jump to where the thing went, when it went somewhere else.','New task, habit, goal and the other add forms now stay put when the keyboard opens, just like Quick capture.','Tap Habit added, Goal added, Project added, Time block added or All-day item added to jump to where it went.','Inbox zero pops in with its check right away, so it no longer looks like it’s loading. The Quick capture type row waits for the keyboard to finish opening before it appears.','The row of types in Quick capture now sits right on top of the keyboard instead of popping up at the top of the screen.','Quick capture opens at full height and stays put while the keyboard comes up, so nothing jumps around as you start typing.','Tasks now opens on All: tasks without a date on top, then everything by date, overdue first.','Quick capture: when it spots what you typed, a green Make it a task (or habit, goal…) button takes you straight there.','While you type in Quick capture, a row of types sits just above the keyboard, so you can file an idea without closing it.','Tap the Saved to Inbox or Task added message to jump to where it went.','Ideas open instantly from the Inbox instead of sliding up blank first. The small Task button on Inbox rows is gone; tap the idea to choose.','Turning an idea into something is clearer: no option is shaded as if it were already picked. Tap any one to open its full form, or just Save to keep it as an idea.','Every module now shows its icon beside its title, the same icon you see for it in lists, so names and icons are easy to learn together.','Cleaner empty-state icon: the check badge now sits in its own gap instead of crossing the card outline, on every page.','The right keyboard for every field: amounts open the decimal pad, counts and days the number pad, phone numbers the phone pad, and links the web keyboard. Return now says Next and jumps to the next field.','New date picker on Today: tap the date for big, easy-to-tap days, month buttons to jump ahead, and shortcuts for Today, Tomorrow, Next Monday and +1 week.','Opening and leaving pages is now a quick, light glide that stays smooth on iPhone, with no freeze mid-slide and no blank flash when going back.','The bottom bar now works like iPhone tabs: one highlight springs smoothly to the tab you tap, with no flicker, no double highlight, and no jump in the labels.','After a pull to refresh, the Up to date pill rides up with the page instead of passing over the date.','Tapping the Tomorrow card switches to tomorrow instantly, with no animation.','The + button goes straight to Quick capture, with no menu in between.','Moving to another day is quicker: the Tomorrow card opens faster, the time grid settles sooner, and a shorter pull at the bottom of Today takes you to the next day.'];
